        <div id="map"></div>
        
        <div class="info-panel">
            <h3>About These Counties</h3>
            <p>During the Ulster Plantation (beginning 1609) and subsequent decades, McCreary families from Scotland settled primarily in these four counties of Ulster. The highlighted counties represent the main areas where Scottish Presbyterian families, including the McCrearys, established communities before many emigrated to North America in the early 18th century.</p>
            
            <div class="county-list">
                <div class="county-item">
                    <strong>County Antrim</strong>
                    <p>Closest to Scotland across the North Channel; major Presbyterian settlement area</p>
                </div>
                <div class="county-item">
                    <strong>County Down</strong>
                    <p>Southeastern Ulster; significant Scottish Lowlander migration</p>
                </div>
                <div class="county-item">
                    <strong>County Donegal</strong>
                    <p>Northwestern Ulster; mixed plantation settlement patterns</p>
                </div>
                <div class="county-item">
                    <strong>County Tyrone</strong>
                    <p>Central Ulster; heart of the plantation scheme</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
